      "message": "I think we may have lost all unit test coverage for these element-wise conversion functions for structures.\n\nThe problem is that I wrote all of the tests using `function` as the \"other\" address space. Now all of the tests that had shared structures needing conversions either:\n- Use SPIR-V 1.3 and therefore use explicit layouts, no conversion needed\n- Use SPIR-V 1.5 and therefore use OpCopyLogical for the conversions\n\nSo it\u0027d probably be better to change these tests to use `workgroup` for the \"other\" address space instead, rather than splitting them into 1.3 vs 1.5 versions. I think having the 1.5 versions of the `foo_SharedWithBar` tests at the top is enough to cover the key difference of \"no type forking\".\n\nSorry, that\u0027s a bunch of test reworking, but this stuff is awkward enough that we should try and keep the unit test coverage.",
